-- --opens specification (seg/WRITING.md, rule 6) for Sphere3Trunc (doc/br-universal.pdf,
-- Lemma s3conn, Proposition trunc4; pi_4 on maps and classes for Theorem final): one
-- entry per declaration, generated from --opened and checked against the note by kind;
-- the same kinds as the S^2 template SphereTruncation / HomotopyGroups in
-- truncation.opens and pi3.opens.  Kinds:
--   types and levels: PtMap -> PtSec, Maps.PMO, Equiv, isEquiv, isContr, isProp, isSet,
--     isConn, isTrunc, Whitehead.fib, O2, O3, the numerals two / three / four / five;
--     HC -> STr.C -> Quot.Q -> Quot.image; GHom, QGrp.G / grp, PiOne.grp, pi3, pi4
--     (pi_4 X = pi_3 (Omega X) by definition);
--   by-definition steps of the text: pi4-map (= pi3-map (loop F)), pi3-map,
--     Induced.hom (pi4-eta: pi4 eta = pi_1 (loop^2 (loop eta))), loopC / pi4C (their
--     -beta / -def lemmas, before the locks), STr.Lift.map and Quot.Descend (LoopC.beta,
--     as Pi3C.beta), hcl, idC, ev3, Equivalences.compose (ev-base-equiv), PtUP.eta,
--     loop2, Simply.to-fib;
--   extras, not steps of the text, as SphereTruncation.Theorem15.c2 in truncation.opens:
--     Maps.D / Maps.loop in Truncate.c4 / c2 (the checker reduces the .1 of a looping
--     before comparing by arguments; documented in s3.opens, not fixed).
